a newer SHA replaces it, because roles run from a host path: a role directory, its `Dockerfile` and the scan worktree must all describe the one commit the tick's jobs use. Editing the host's working tree therefore changes nothing on a running controller, with one exception: a local `paused: true` is honoured (see the kill switch), and only that key is read locally. A merged change applies on the next tick without a pull. Symlinks and submodules under the role directories are rejected, and a config that cannot be fetched or does not validate counts as paused. If `origin/main` cannot be loaded at startup, `ard serve` starts paused instead of exiting, posts the load error to the status issue once per distinct error, and retries every tick; no loop runs until a config has loaded. `ard config check` validates the working tree, for authoring; `ard config check --ref <ref>` validates a commit of the local checkout (for example `--ref origin/main` after `git fetch`) without fetching.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\nindex 88795e2..182720a 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ func snapshot(t *testing.T, dir string) map[string]string {\n \treturn m\n }\n \n-var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n+var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanner